From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:27:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] block-nbd: give the slot of a cancelled request back

When the connection is disabled, __cancel_req() completed the sent and
pending requests but left them on their list, out of the free list:
nr_free_count never came back up, and a second tdnbd_disable_locked()
(from the close paths) completed the same requests again.

Move the request back to the free list when it is cancelled, and forget
curr_reply_req, which could point to a slot given back if the connection
is lost in the middle of a reply.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/block-nbd.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block-nbd.c b/drivers/block-nbd.c
index 817174f8..20cc6738 100644
--- a/drivers/block-nbd.c
+++ b/drivers/block-nbd.c
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ tdnbd_fdreceiver_stop()
 }
 
 static void
-__cancel_req(int i, struct td_nbd_request *pos, int e)
+__cancel_req(struct tdnbd_data *prv, int i, struct td_nbd_request *pos, int e)
 {
 	INFO("Entry %d: handle='%s' type=%d, len=%d: %s",
 	     i, pos->nreq.handle, ntohs(pos->nreq.type), ntohl(pos->nreq.len), strerror(e));
@@ -215,6 +215,11 @@ __cancel_req(int i, struct td_nbd_request *pos, int e)
 		pos->timeout_event = -1;
 	}
 
+	/* give the slot back so that it is not cancelled twice and
+	 * td_pending() does not report it forever */
+	list_move(&pos->queue, &prv->free_reqs);
+	prv->nr_free_count++;
+
 	td_complete_request(pos->treq, e);
 }
 
@@ -233,11 +238,13 @@ tdnbd_disable_locked(struct tdnbd_data *prv, int e)
 
 	INFO("NBD client cancelling sent reqs");
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(pos, q, &prv->sent_reqs, queue)
-		__cancel_req(i++, pos, e);
+		__cancel_req(prv, i++, pos, e);
 
 	INFO("NBD client cancelling pending reqs");
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(pos, q, &prv->pending_reqs, queue)
-		__cancel_req(i++, pos, e);
+		__cancel_req(prv, i++, pos, e);
+
+	prv->curr_reply_req = NULL;
 
 	INFO("Setting state to dead");
 	prv->state = TDNBD_DEAD;
